katie: FYI customer reported our troubleshooting page examples failed when pasted into their app. opening thread to coordinate a tiny docs PR.
sam: dropped the curl they used; getting a reproducible 429 on staging. response:
```
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Retry-After: 4
{"error":"rate_limited"}
```
sam: the JS snippet in the page still shows `maxRetries` which is no longer accepted by the SDK (it now reads `retryCount`). that breaks copy/paste.
olga: ok i can update the snippet to include both names and mark `retryCount` as preferred. i'll also swap the naive sleep example for a tiny backoff helper with jitter.
nisha: +1. please add a short migration table at top: `maxRetries -> retryCount`, `timeoutMs -> requestTimeout`, `contextWindow -> maxContextTokens`. customers keep pasting old keys.
jeremy: also recommend honoring Retry-After header before client-side sleep. the current text encourages an immediate retry which just amplifies the problem. add a sentence: "If Retry-After present, delay at least that long before retrying."
olga: draft helper (JS) to include:
```js
async function retryWithBackoff(fn, retries = 3) {
  let attempt = 0;
  while (attempt <= retries) {
    try { return await fn(); }
    catch (err) {
      if (attempt === retries) throw err;
      // honor Retry-After if present on err.response
      const ra = err?.response?.headers?.['retry-after'];
      if (ra) {
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, Number(ra) * 1000));
      } else {
        const delay = Math.pow(2, attempt) * 100 + Math.floor(Math.random() * 100);
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delay));
      }
      attempt++;
    }
  }
}
```

katie: ok keep the helper compact and add a short language-agnostic note recommending exponential backoff + jitter and to prefer honoring Retry-After.
sam: small ask: add a one-line troubleshooting checklist at the top of the page: "If you see repeated 429s: 1) verify SDK parameter names (see migration table), 2) honor Retry-After, 3) use exponential backoff with jitter, 4) for streams: handle partial payloads/abort logs."
nisha: on streams: add a simple log-match example to help support triage: `stream aborted: requestTimeout=\d+ms` so customers and support can grep logs. mention that timeouts may cut the stream mid-message.
jeremy: docs-ci: PR link please when opened. also add a single line redirect from the old anchor path to the new error-ref page so existing links keep working.
olga: will open a small PR that replaces the naive sleep, inserts migration table, adds the helper and checklist, and includes redirect. will keep the change tiny.
